    schema:about "Pomacanthus semicirculatus juvenile pigment stripes (model target) & Myxococcus xanthus rippling cell populations (specimen)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: Individual-cell C-signal contact-reversal mechanics or 3D fruiting-body stalk elevation",
        "does_not_claim: Reproduction of PNAS 1999 Fig. 4-5 anisotropic 2D growth (1.8e-4 / 2.2e-4) or Fig. 8 Lengyel-Epstein adult stripe-to-spot transition",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Computer-vision segmentation of the Myxococcus xanthus specimen (`chemotactic_pattern_specimen.jpg`, CC BY-SA 4.0): 4 fruiting-body spot aggregates and 362 rippling stripe spacings (74.10 um mean wavelength via the 500 um = 125 px scale bar)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Generic Keller-Segel chemotaxis-logistic 1D/2D IMEX pseudospectral solvers (stationary s in {1, 2, 4, 8}, subcritical control chi = 3.0, growing-domain kymograph 1 -> 2 -> 4, 2D cubic stripes vs quadratic spots) and a slime-trail nematic tensor Q with mobility M = I + aQ tested by a chi-drop hysteresis protocol (grow at 6.2, hold at 4.0 / 4.4)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: PNAS 1999 Fig. 3 system integrated on a uniformly growing surface of revolution (1D line, cylinder K = 0, spindle K lambda_c^2 = 0.69) with a Laplace-Beltrami eigenbasis solver, fully implicit diffusion + Jacobian + 2r dilution, explicit clipped kinetics and chemotactic flux; stripe counts 3 -> 6 -> 12 on flat flanks (doubling scale ratio 2.03), 3 -> 6 -> 8 on the spindle; chi_0 sweep over two orders of magnitude",
        "reported_in_source: Balagam & Igoshin (2015) trail-following alignment of gliding M. xanthus cells",
        "reported_in_source: Keller & Segel (1970) J. Theor. Biol. 26:399-415 chemotactic flux cross-diffusion -div(n chi(c) grad(c)) and its linear instability; Crampin, Gaffney & Maini (1999) growing-domain dilution and mode doubling; Ermentrout (1991) stripe-vs-spot selection",
        "reported_in_source: Painter, Maini & Othmer (1999) PNAS 96(10):5549-5554 Eqs. (1)-(3): Kondo-Asai piecewise-linear Turing morphogens u, v with chemotactic iridophores n, chi(u) = chi_0/(k+u)^2, chi_0 < 0, on an exponentially growing domain L(t) = 11 exp(1e-4 t) (Fig. 3: 3-peak juvenile pattern; Fig. 1 / Kondo & Asai 1995: 3 -> 6 -> 12 stripes at 2, 6, 12 months)",
        "transfer_boundary: The Keller-Segel rippling model and slime-trail tensor are mapped to M. xanthus rippling ridges; the tensor is a continuum closure, not an agent-based trail model",
        "transfer_boundary: The PNAS 1999 iridophore model is compared against Kondo & Asai's stripe COUNTS (3, 6, 12) only; no Pomacanthus photograph is vendored, so curvature-dependent stripe geometry is not validated against a fish specimen" ;
    pk:anatomicalStructure "Turing pigment stripe / ocellus wavelength in Myxococcus xanthus" ;
    pk:aristotelianEfficientCause "1. Chemical Turing / RD" ;
    pk:aristotelianMegistonGenos "IV. Protista & Monera" ;
