<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Painter, Maini & Othmer (1999) Pomacanthus Turing-chemotaxis stripe doubling on a growing curved flank & Keller-Segel rippling with slime-trail tensor — Model fidelity to source: 95/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "For the first time implements the actual PNAS 1999 model: `PMO_PARAMS`/`pmo_kinetics` (L546-574, clipped Kondo-Asai kinetics with (u*, v*) = (3, 2.5) verified in the self-test), `pmo_turing_stability` (L575-615) reproducing the Turing conditions and three-stripe mode selection, and `simulate_pomacanthus_growing_surface` (L703-856) on a growing surface of revolution with metric g = s^2 g_0, Laplace-Beltrami eigenbasis (`_surface_eigenbasis`, L639-665), conservative chemotactic divergence (L666-683) and 2r morphogen dilution. The slime-trail tensor (`simulate_slime_trail_ks`, L891-997) adds a nematic closure with mobility on both D_n and chi. 7 Lean theorems (0 sorrys) cover Laws 1-6. Deductions: the 2D KS stripe regime (`simulate_2d_stripe_vs_spot`, L466-541) still imposes a 6.2/3.8 x/y chemotactic anisotropy to obtain stripes (disclosed in the docstring L478-483 and Panel D label) rather than deriving it from the trail tensor; the Fig. 4 anisotropic RC/DV growth and Fig. 8 Lengyel-Epstein transition are not implemented." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1999-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting.py L478–L483: Docstring discloses that the 2D stripe regime imposes a 6.2/3.8 x/y chemotactic anisotropy (not derived from the trail tensor) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/4d5512d/1999-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting.py#L478-L483>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-model-fidelity-2>,
