<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Painter, Maini & Othmer (1999) Pomacanthus Turing-chemotaxis stripe doubling on a growing curved flank & Keller-Segel rippling with slime-trail tensor — Morphometric validation: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1121-1299) returns 13 reference-anchored measurements: the 5 Pass 2 quantities (re-attributed) plus initial stripe count (3 vs 3), cylinder final count (12 vs 12), doubling scale ratio (2.03 vs 2.0), spindle final count (8 vs 12, reported as a curvature effect), iridophore contrast vs quasi-static flux-balance estimate (0.201 vs 0.117, ratio 1.73), chi_0 Spearman monotonicity (1.0), Law-6 threshold vs hysteresis bracket midpoint (4.22 vs 4.2) and trail/isotropic amplitude ratio (2.95 vs null 1.0). Deductions: the contrast measurement is an order-of-magnitude check only (the cells are not quasi-static during splitting), and the spindle count disagrees with its reference by 4 stripes." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
