<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-19-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-audit-v3-painter-chemotactic-stripe-splitting-10> a schema:QuantitativeValue,
        pk1:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "iridophore stripe contrast n_max/n_min - 1 at chi_0 = -1e-4 vs quasi-static flux-balance (Boltzmann) estimate" ;
    dct:description "1D Fig. 3 run at s = 5.2; bound exp(-(chi_0/D_n)(1/(k+u_min) - 1/(k+u_max))) - 1 with u in [0.402, 5.177]" ;
    dct:source "flux balance D_n n' = n chi(u) u' integrated with chi(u) = chi_0/(k+u)^2 (PNAS 1999 Eq. 3 with Othmer & Stevens 1997 sensitivity) for a STATIC morphogen pattern; PNAS 1999: 'movement of the cells is much slower than diffusion of molecules'" ;
    rdfs:comment "observed/quasi-static = 1.727; iridophores accumulate at u minima because chi_0 < 0 (repellent). The ratio exceeds 1 because the slow cells (D_n = 5e-4) are swept by the moving u peaks during the 6 -> 12 splitting at s = 4.44, so n is not quasi-static at s = 5.2; same-order agreement is the tested quantity" ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy "script" ;
    schema:about "Pomacanthus semicirculatus juvenile pigment stripes (model target) & Myxococcus xanthus rippling cell populations (specimen)" ;
    schema:error 7.27273e+01 ;
    schema:targetValue 1.166e-01 ;
    schema:unitText "dimensionless density contrast" ;
    schema:value 2.014e-01 .

